{
 "_what": "enemy type id (placement byte +0x02) -> creature name, with the evidence and how sure we are",
 "_key": "The TYPE ID is the identifier, not the HP-table row. Every (type, variant) pair resolves to a real model file romdata.afs/E<type>_<variant>.NBD, and the model numbering is shared by both discs.",
 "_no_names_on_disc": "No English CREATURE name is reachable from an enemy type id on either disc - not in the scenario data, not in SLPM_654.28 / SLPM_656.92, not in BIN/2.DAT or PROG/GAME.BIN. Creature names are necessarily external; the disc gives identity. Both executables DO carry an array of English personal names (90 on File 1, 93 on File 2: MACDOWELL, HUNK, AXEMAN, DOROTHY, Mr.RED ...) and it is worth saying plainly that this is NOT that table. It is the extended character roster, indexed by a character-slot key rather than by type id - see extracted_data/characters.json for the disassembly. A few of its entries are also enemies, AXEMAN among them, which is exactly why it reads like a lead; it still yields no type id.",
 "_tiers": {
  "forced": "the Evil Resource rosters of the levels holding this type leave exactly one candidate",
  "supported": "consistent with every roster it can be checked against, but not narrowed to one",
  "unverified": "named, but a level holding this type does not list the creature - the rosters are incomplete, so this is a lead, not a rejection",
  "unnamed": "no defensible name; shown as \"Type N\""
 },
 "_sources": [
  "extracted_data/combat/enemy-placements.json (disc)",
  "Data Resources/Evil Resource html downloads/Levels (per-level rosters)",
  "romdata.afs E<type>_<variant>.NBD (mounted ISOs)"
 ],
 "_withdrawn": {
  "Flying Bug": "matched 38 HP-table rows and landed on nine unrelated type ids (4, 46, 48, 54, 57, 60, 61, 62, 63) whose HP runs from 1 to 5,000. No Evil Resource roster lists a \"Flying Bug\".",
  "Web Spinner": "the creature is Giant Spider (type 7); \"Web Spinner\" is not an Evil Resource name.",
  "Scissor Tail on type 22": "Below Freezing Point holds type 22 and lists no scissor creature. Type 22 is the Hunter; type 36 is the scissor creature.",
  "Cerberus on type 65": "Wild Things lists no Zombie Dog. Type 2 is the dog; type 65 is Wild Things-only.",
  "Ivy Plant": "neither Flashback nor Wild Things lists any plant, and the label sat on two type ids (34 and 35) at once.",
  "Dorothy": "not an Evil Resource name, and Flashback's roster does not list it. Type 51 waits for a better source."
 },
